# userdirs.schema — which layer may decide each key of the `userdirs` subsystem.
#
# Read by /usr/lib/w/w-conf-lib.sh (and its Python twin) during the load
# pass; a user-layer assignment to a `system` key is dropped with a warning, and
# `wconf_set` refuses to write it in the first place. See w-conf.md.
#
# Format: <KEY>\t<scope>       scope: system | user | both
#   system — root domain: the admin (or fleet policy) decides, per machine.
#   user   — the logged-in user may override it in ~/.config/w/userdirs.conf.
#   both   — either layer may speak; the usual priority order applies.
#
# The folders are one user's own, renamed by that user's own login step, so the
# key is theirs — no polkit anywhere in this subsystem (the Hub calls
# `w-userdirs` directly, as it calls `w-session`). A fleet that wants to fix it
# still can: policy.d sits above the user layer and locks the setter.

LOCALIZE	user
